## Why This Is Asked
Tests API design discipline, latency considerations, and privacy handling for a live scoring service. It requires concrete endpoints, data fields, and rollout strategies rather than abstract concepts.

## Key Concepts
- Deterministic scoring with consistent model behavior across regions
- Privacy-first design with masked user identifiers
- Canary rollout and backpressure mechanisms for safe deployment
- Observability: latency tracking, error monitoring, drift detection

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeScore(features, salt) {
  let h = 0;
  for(const f of features) {
    h = ((h << 5) - h) + f.charCodeAt(0);
    h = h & h;
  }
  return Math.abs(h + salt) % 1000;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a scalable, fault-tolerant streaming pipeline with privacy controls for distributed data.

## Key Concepts

- Streaming ingestion with exactly-once guarantees
- Replay protection using nonces and signatures
- Per-region DP budgets and auditability
- Fault tolerance for intermittent connectivity

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo idempotent sink
function ingestEvent(event, store) {
  const key = event.device_id + ':' + event.nonce;
  if (store.exists(key)) return;
  store.write(key, event.score);
  // update region aggregates atomically
}
```

